   "host_assumptions": [
    "Host assumption, not user-confirmed: primary human fibroblasts, dermal or lung, on tissue-culture plastic unless an arm changes the substrate.",
    "Host assumption: recombinant TGF-beta1 2-5 ng/mL for 48-72 h, then washout into TGF-beta1-free medium.",
    "Host assumption: the phenotype is read as alpha-SMA in stress fibres plus contractility, days after washout.",
    "Donor, passage, serum level, substrate stiffness and the exact day after washout are not fixed and must be recorded as variables.",
    "No source in this pack measures residual exogenous TGF-beta1 after washout or how long it lasts; every residual-ligand expectation here is assumption, not pack evidence.",
    "No source in this pack tests paracrine transfer after washout; the cell-to-cell predictions rest on mechanism analogy.",
    "Cross-species and cross-cell-type sources (rat cardiac fibroblasts, valvular interstitial cells, CAFs, MSCs) are candidate mechanisms, not evidence about human fibroblasts.",
    "Assumption to be tested, not granted: the pan-TGF-beta neutralising antibody and the TGF-beta-RI kinase inhibitor fully block acute TGF-beta1 signalling at the doses used.",
    "Assumption to be tested, not granted: the medium TGF-beta1 assay detects carried-over ligand at the concentrations that would matter biologically.",
    "Assumption to be tested, not granted: alpha-SMA protein turnover is fast enough that a day-5 signal reflects ongoing expression rather than protein made during treatment."
